<</Title(USER JOURNEY)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 463 0 R/First 471 0 R/Last 472 0 R/Count -2/Next 464 0 R>>
endobj

468 0 obj
<</Title(Manual fallback wastes class time \204 when the scanner fails, the professor has to open their own app and mark each student one by one, consuming 5\20510 minutes of teaching time per session)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 463 0 R/Prev 465 0 R/Next 466 0 R>>
endobj

469 0 obj
<</Title(No mechanism to prevent proxy in the manual flow \204 when professors mark attendance manually, they often go by a quick visual sweep, which is vulnerable to the exact proxy attendance the facial recognition was meant to eliminate)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 466 0 R/Next 470 0 R>>
endobj

470 0 obj
<</Title(The core issue is over-reliance on a single point of failure \204 the entire process depends on the camera working perfectly, and when it doesn't, there is no graceful, fast,alternative)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 466 0 R/Prev 469 0 R>>
endobj

